    "value": "No — Kentucky's constitution excludes convicted felons from office generally (relievable only by a gubernatorial pardon), but the U.S. Constitution's own qualifications for Congress (age, citizenship, residency) can't be added to by any state, so this doesn't reach U.S. House or Senate candidates",
